                                "sense_id": "95e2293e-4558-331b-b307-1979f08508d9",
                                "text": "Jenny was sining on the closed lid of the toilet, her long legs stretched out in front of her so that he could treat the cuts with mercurochrome."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb07edaf-42bc-4bae-8fe1-cd863a31c5ee",
                                "sense_id": "95e2293e-4558-331b-b307-1979f08508d9",
                                "text": "While expounding the other day on the lost antiseptic mercurochrome, I mentioned that vaccines once contained an antibacterial and antifungal agent called thimerosal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "363a885e-2c3d-4f92-a3e7-fefdf327e300",
                                "sense_id": "95e2293e-4558-331b-b307-1979f08508d9",
                                "text": "Oocyst counts in mosquitoes were made 7 days postinfection on midguts dissected from 30 gravid females and then stained with 0.5% mercurochrome."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48aaf3e4-287e-4685-81d3-daf81a2217a4",
                                "sense_id": "95e2293e-4558-331b-b307-1979f08508d9",
                                "text": "Then the doctor came bustling in, brown-mustached, blue-tied, spectacled, carrying a tan bag, and behind him followed the two ambulance men, one with a thatch of flaming red hair and the other with a stain of mercurochrome on his jacket-sleeve."
                            }
                        ]
